      "message": "After trying it, it\u0027s a lot of effort to use it for a lazy person, e.g.:\n[a] the unresolved output cannot be cut\u0026paste in the annotation file without reformatting\n[b] I need to open each source file mentioned\n[c] there is a lot of duplications in the annotations\n (if my function pointer is called 15 times and can resolve to 4 functions, I have to put 15x(4+1) \u003d 75 lines)\n[d] at the end of the day, I probably want to re-use my annotations, so rather than having a large annotation json file, I probably want to put chunks of it in each directory and the tool re-constructs the whole file.\n\nFor [a] and [b], maybe rather than printing:\n\"-\u003e ccd_password_digest [common/ccd_config.c:262] 511a2\"\nI need an option (or the default) to generate a useful template for my annotation file, e.g.:\n\"\"\"\n   ccd_password_digest[common/ccd_config.c:262]:\n   - HASH_update(\u0026sha, config.password_salt, sizeof(config.password_salt)); @511a2\n\"\"\"",
